config VS_AP_RANDOM_PASSWORD
	bool "Generate a random eight-character AP password"
	default n
	depends on LVX_USE_DEMO_CONTEST2026_264_VELASIGHT
	---help---
		Give the SoftAP an eight-character alphanumeric passphrase drawn from
		the hardware TRNG instead of the fixed VS_AP_PASSWORD.
		Disabled by default while AP provisioning is in testing.

		The passphrase is drawn once and persisted to /mnt/sdnand/prov/APPW.BIN,
		then read back into memory at startup, so the hotspot keeps the same
		password across reboots and across STA/AP switches.  It has to: the
		password is shown on the device's screen and typed into a phone, and
		redrawing it on every AP start would invalidate whatever the user
		already saved there.  Entering AP mode when a stored passphrase exists
		performs no storage access at all.

		A new passphrase is drawn only when there is none stored, when the
		stored record fails its CRC or range checks, or when the user asks:
		holding 下一条 (VS_KEY_NEXT) for VS_LONG_PRESS_MS on the SoftAP page
		restarts the hotspot with a fresh passphrase and saves it.  The page
		advertises that key while the gesture is available.  The gesture is
		tied to this option because with a fixed VS_AP_PASSWORD there is
		nothing to reset -- restarting the AP would hand back the same string
		and only cost the user their connection.

