config VS_VOICE_PROMPT_MAX_BYTES
	int "VelaSight idle assistant prompt budget (bytes)"
	default 32768
	range 2048 131072
	depends on LVX_USE_DEMO_CONTEST2026_264_VELASIGHT

config VS_VOICE_RESP_MAX_BYTES
	int "VelaSight idle assistant model response buffer (bytes)"
	default 32768
	range 8192 131072
	depends on LVX_USE_DEMO_CONTEST2026_264_VELASIGHT

config VS_VOICE_RECORD_MAX_MS
	int "VelaSight idle assistant listening window (ms)"
	default 15000
	range 3000 60000
	depends on LVX_USE_DEMO_CONTEST2026_264_VELASIGHT
	---help---
		How long one utterance is recorded when the user does not end it
		with the confirm key.

		This is the only thing that ends an utterance automatically.  The
		assistant deliberately has no local speech detector: an energy
		threshold calibrated for a different microphone sat above normal
		speech at this board's gain and silently discarded whole
		recordings, so ending a round is left to the confirm key, the back
		key, and the recognizer's own verdict on whether there was
		anything to transcribe.

		It therefore serves two purposes: a bound on how long a user who
		walked away is listened to before the conversation is written to
		chat history, and a safety net if a key event is ever missed.
		Because a truncated question is worse than a short wait, prefer
		raising this over lowering it.

